# ─── Working files, not deliverables ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything ignored here is either regenerable from the scripts in this repo
# or a source file whose encoded output already lives in build/assets/.

# Python environment — recreate with the commands in README.md
.venv/

# Raw generation downloads, rendered frames, and source recordings.
# The encoded results the site actually serves are in build/assets/.
gen/
render/frames/
render/*.mp4
*.mov

# Playwright verification screenshots — regenerate with `python shoot.py`
shots/

# ─── Capture archive: keep the words, drop the weight ────────────────────────
# The recovered copy is the valuable part and it lives in the .txt files.
# The rendered HTML, full-page screenshots and third-party Shopify bundles
# add ~85MB and tell you nothing the text and the brief don't already.
original/assets/
original/screenshots/
original/pages/**/*.html
original/archive/*.html

# Working image crops used while building — not referenced by the site
inventory/slices/
inventory/imgs/
inventory/ath/

# ─── Design reference: keep the specs and source art, drop the comps ─────────
# The CLAUDE-INSTRUCTIONS.md files and the overlay SVGs are what the build was
# made from. The reference PNGs are 5MB comps each (~100MB total).
design-reference/**/*.png
design-reference/applied-motion/
design-reference/visual-references/

# ─── Internal, not for a public repo ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The huddle transcript is unredacted internal conversation. This GitHub repo
# is public — it does not belong in it.
Slack Transcript*/

# Team-supplied source media. The photos are small enough to keep; the clips
# are 100MB of raw recordings whose encoded output lands in build/assets/.
source-media/*.mov

# macOS noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Scratch logs from the capture scripts
*.log
